    {
      "id": "50t90l3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Carbohydrates"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "otyudw1",
      "content": "• Carbohydrates are the main source of energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "el9s71y",
      "content": "• They are broken down into glucose."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bmritoq",
      "content": "• Stored in the liver and muscles as glycogen."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "A balanced diet provides all essential nutrients in appropriate proportions to maintain health, growth, and proper physiological function.",
      "id": "h2742xk"
    },
    {
      "id": "zlfvh3u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Proteins"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wmgasck",
      "content": "• Proteins are essential for growth and repair of tissues."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zkhipbn",
      "content": "• They are composed of amino acids."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bbyzsx5",
      "content": "• Important for enzymes and hormones."
    },
    {
      "id": "8vmbb90",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Fats"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ur7hz93",
      "content": "• Fats provide twice as much energy as carbohydrates."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3l2qve7",
      "content": "• They help in absorption of vitamins A, D, E and K."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kkvf7vb",
      "content": "• They protect internal organs."
    },
    {
