    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Vitamin C (Ascorbic Acid) is water-soluble and heat-sensitive; it gets destroyed easily during cooking.",
        "Kwashiorkor is caused by severe protein deficiency and causes edema, whereas Marasmus is caused by deficiency of both proteins and total calories.",
        "Iodine deficiency causes Goitre due to thyroid enlargement, while Vitamin D deficiency leads to Rickets in children and Osteomalacia in adults."
      ],
      "id": "b4oeyd6"
    },
    {
      "id": "ecnm6gb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.Important Exam Points"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z8gpxyf",
      "content": "• Carbohydrates are the main source of energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0di1ux9",
      "content": "• Proteins are body-building nutrients."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0xdozpp",
      "content": "• Vitamin D deficiency causes rickets."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6e57n3a",
      "content": "• Iron deficiency causes anemia."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "euj5sjk",
      "content": "• Iodine deficiency causes goitre."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "945jvit",
      "content": "• Protein deficiency causes kwashiorkor."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xzn3efq",
      "content": "• Vitamin C deficiency causes scurvy."
    }
  ],
